{"id":1045,"date":"2020-11-18T20:25:47","date_gmt":"2020-11-19T04:25:47","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1045"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:42","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:42","slug":"build-the-sumo-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-sumo-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Build the Sumo Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22160b90a87\" name=\"6a22160b90a87\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Attach the motors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Attach two short L-frames to a blueboard, and then make a mirror image with two more L-frames on another blueboard. Next, attach two short standoffs to each blueboard, and again, make sure they are mirror images of each other.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the motor casings to the L-frames. Make sure the backs of the motors are facing each other!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1046&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1047&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22160b90bab\" name=\"6a22160b90bab\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The body<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Assemble two sets of very long standoffs by attaching one short standoff, one nut, one long standoff, and one short standoff.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the two standoffs you just made to the blueboard with nuts. They should be in the fourth column and in the first and fourth rows.<\/li>\n<li>Add four more long standoffs to the blueboard using nuts.<\/li>\n<li>Attach long L-frames to each of the three sets of standoffs using short bolts.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1048&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1049&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1050&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1051&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22160b90c11\" name=\"6a22160b90c11\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add the battery pack and motor structures<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Attach a 7-hole silver frame to the back of a battery pack. This will allow you to bolt the battery pack to the body of your Sumo Bot.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the battery pack to the long L-frame attached to the very long standoffs.<\/li>\n<li>Using the bolts and the four short standoffs on the blueboards with the motors, attach the top body to the bottom body.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1052&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1053&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1054&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22160b90c71\" name=\"6a22160b90c71\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Smart Inventor Board and wheels<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Attach two long bolts to the Smart Inventor Board with nuts and nylon nuts. Pay attention to the placement of the bolts!<\/li>\n<li>Use four short standoffs to make two stacked standoffs, and then bolt those to the Smart Inventor Board. The standoffs should be on the outside of the long bolts.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the Smart Inventor Board to your Sumo Bot using the long standoffs and bolts.<\/li>\n<li>Put wheels on each of your motors with black screws. The wheels will stay attached without the screws!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1055&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1056&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1057&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1058&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22160b90cc9\" name=\"6a22160b90cc9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The pushers<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Attach two long standoffs to each of the long L-frames at the front of the Sumo Bot.<\/li>\n<li>Attach a long bolt to each of the two horn brackets with a nut.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the horn brackets to the standoffs at the front. These will be your pushers, so make sure they&#8217;re secure!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1059&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1060&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1061&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22160b90d31\" name=\"6a22160b90d31\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wire the Sumo Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You&#8217;re done building your Sumo Bot! Now you need to wire it.<\/p>\n<p>Hold your robot so that the Smart Inventor Board is facing you:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The motor on the right is M1.<\/li>\n<li>The motor on the left is M2.<\/li>\n<li>Attach their wires to the SmartInventor board where it&#8217;s marked M1, M2, M3, and M4.<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that the red wires are the in the negative position (facing the inside) and that the black wires are in the positive position (facing the outside)!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1062&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 Attach the motors [vc_column_text] Attach two short L-frames to a blueboard, and then make a mirror image with two more L-frames on another blueboard. Next, attach two&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-sumo-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1733,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2168,2171,2189,2187,2188],"class_list":["post-1045","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-sensors","lesson-tag-sumo","lesson-tag-sumo-bot","module-sumo","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1045","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-jso